          "signal": "step",
          "gpio": "23",
          "function_input_key": "x_step_pin",
          "notes": null
        },
        {
          "id": "x-axis-motor-enable",
          "signal": "enable",
          "gpio": "10",
          "function_input_key": "gantry_enable_pin",
          "notes": "Shared ENABLE for both CoreXY TB6600 drivers. ENA- to GND with PUL-/DIR-, ENA+ here. Active LOW: energising a TB6600's opto DISABLES it, so the pin is pulled low to run the motors. Confirmed by releasing the pin - it falls to the pull-down and the motors energise. Note GPIO 10 is SPI0 MOSI, so enabling SPI would claim it."
        },
